# What `gcloud run deploy --source .` uploads to the Cloud Build staging
# bucket. Without this file gcloud falls back to .gitignore, which here covers
# only .env.yaml and __pycache__ — so every deploy was shipping ~3 GB of
# eval_data/ and test_pdfs/ to GCS before Docker's own .dockerignore threw
# them away again. .env.yaml is repeated here on purpose: it is the one file
# that must never reach a bucket, and the fallback that used to exclude it
# stops applying the moment this file exists.
.git/
.gitignore
.DS_Store
.env
.env.yaml
.keys/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
local.log
eval_data/
test_pdfs/
evals/fixtures/
outputs/
